la pycyn cusku di'e



It may be only that
{ka [bridi]} is shorter than {se ckaji le nu [bridi]}

At least we have a clear definition for the competing meaning
for {ka}. I suggest {tu'o} instead of {le} for the definition
though, since probably we don't want this in-mind selection
as part of {ka}.

I still prefer the other ka:



{ka ce'u broda} = {se ckaji tu'o broda}





The extension of {ka ce'u broda} is presumably a set of things, lo'i
broda, in fact.

No, that would be the extension of And's {poi'i ce'u broda},
see http://nuzban.wiw.org/wiki/index.php?poi%27i

I also proposed using {se ka} for this.



mu'o mi'e xorxes




